<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>When it is <m>0{8}:0{0}</m> GMT, the local time on a ship is <m>{10}:{40}</m>. Find the ship's longitude.</p><p><fillin characters="5" name="ans1"/> <m>^\circ</m> [ E | W ]  </p></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>The ship's clock is ahead by <m>{160}</m> minutes. Each degree of longitude is <m>4</m> minutes of time, so the ship is <m>{160} \div 4 = {40}^\circ</m> east of Greenwich. The ship's longitude is <m>{40}^\circ\,\mathrm{E}</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>40</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p>E</p></answer>
</stack-static>